Z||000000||Dumba$$||10-03-2001||02:14 PM||||im looking to lower my 86 se 1" to 1-1/2" <BR>who has the best spring for the $$ <BR>i would like to keep as nice and smooth of a ride as possible<BR>gtbastard was telling me that intraxx had some cheep ones what do you all think??<BR><P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE <BR>98 acura cl 3.0<P>4.9 caddy engine for sale 30,000 miles complete with bubba joes mounts!!  $850<P>if it dont go, put a fart can, and clear taillights on it!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||10-03-2001||02:28 PM||||Any lowering spring set will stiffen your ride. Your best bet to retain the ride quality is to use the Street Dreams lowering spindles and adjustable coil-overs in the rear.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DreXteR||10-03-2001||02:37 PM||||Well I have the Intraxx but havent finish the car yet. I did the front and man it is salmed to the floor. <P>DreX<p>[This message has been edited by DreXteR (edited 10-03-2001).]||||reg||10
